:name: U400 §9b inject-and-run -- autonomous door_unlock under the real scheduler
:description: Boots the Aqara U400 firmware to a running FreeRTOS (radio/I2C/fs stubbed), then INJECTS a real mbus "door_unlock" publish exactly as the producer sub_8072174 does (sub_80c8f68("pid_motor","door_unlock",&payload,8)) and observes the prio-31 pid_motor CONSUMER task sub_80718FC autonomously WAKE under the real scheduler, dequeue the message, call the unlock actuator sub_80714F4, pass the "already-unlocked" guard sub_8070818, and reach the motor DRIVE function sub_806DA24. This is the §9b result: the actuation code path is reached AUTONOMOUSLY (not hand-stitched). Still emulation -- no motor model, so physical motion is unobservable; this proves code-path reachability under the genuine RTOS scheduler.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESULT (2026-07-23, this branch). Trace excerpt (end of run):
#   TRAP r0=0x0                                  ; injected sub_80c8f68 publish returned success
#   CONSUMER_GOT_MSG                             ; blocked consumer sub_80718FC woke & dequeued
#   *** UNLOCK_ACTUATOR sub_80714f4 arg0=0xC8 ** ; consumer called unlock actuator w/ injected speed
#   UNLOCK_GUARD sub_8070818                     ; already-unlocked guard ran (returned proceed)
#   *** DRIVE sub_806da24 ***                    ; reached the motor drive function
# arg0=0xC8 == the speed byte in the injected payload -> proves the consumer processed OUR message.
#
# WHY THIS RECIPE (hard-won; see HANDOFF-NATIVE-DEBUG.md §9b):
#  * 3 boot stubs get to a running RTOS with the consumer created + blocked on its mailbox
#    semaphore (handle 0x20034090). See u400-rtos-boot.resc.
#  * The FreeRTOS scheduler tick runs WITHOUT BURTC (PendSV @0x08006430 fires ~32/s; the tick
#    uses SysRTC/SysTick, NOT the BURTC HAL timebase). So a readied task CAN be switched to.
#  * WITHOUT BURTC the HAL delay sub_80e2d7a busy-spins forever at 0x80e2d98 (reads unmodeled
#    BURTC CNT @0x50064020) -- this spin is a RELIABLE, actively-executing, thread-mode injection
#    point. (Modeling BURTC removes this spin but then boot hangs at a b. @0x80d4904 -- a further
#    unmodeled dependency; not needed for this test.)
#  * The mbus publish sub_80c8f68 gives the mailbox semaphore via a TASK path (sub_8011554) or an
#    ISR path (sub_80111d0) chosen by xPortIsInsideInterrupt (sub_80e2cb4, reads IPSR). Injecting
#    ONLY when the CPU is in thread mode (ICSR VECTACTIVE==0) forces the task path, which requests
#    a proper yield. We also force PENDSVSET in the trap for good measure.
#  * Renode halts the core on b./WFI "wait" states, so paused-PC injection won't execute; a HOOK at
#    an actively-executing instruction is required -> the console spin at 0x80e2d98.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

$bin?=@/home/chen/aliro-renode/matter/aliro-u400/firmware/U400_primary_target.elf
$vtor?=0x08006000
include @scripts/silabs-vuln/boot_mg24.resc
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString "scratch: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x30000000 { size: 0x1000 }"

# --- boot-to-running-RTOS stubs (see u400-rtos-boot.resc for rationale) ---
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3d60 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3d62 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e46 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e48 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e56 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e58 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e86 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e88 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e96 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e98 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3dce 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3dd0 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x803266c 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x803266e 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x804b8e0 0x2001
sysbus WriteWord 0x804b8e2 0x4770

# return trap (b . landing pad for the injected publish's LR)
sysbus WriteWord 0x30000100 0xe7fe

# --- observation hooks (the §9b evidence) ---
sysbus.cpu AddHook 0x80c8ea2 "self.ErrorLog('9B: CONSUMER_GOT_MSG (sub_80718FC dequeued the mbus message)')"
sysbus.cpu AddHook 0x80714f4 "self.ErrorLog('9B: *** UNLOCK_ACTUATOR sub_80714f4 CALLED, arg0(speed)=0x{0:X} ***'.format(self.GetRegister(0).RawValue))"
sysbus.cpu AddHook 0x8070818 "self.ErrorLog('9B: UNLOCK_GUARD sub_8070818 (already-unlocked check)')"
sysbus.cpu AddHook 0x806da24 "self.ErrorLog('9B: *** DRIVE sub_806da24 REACHED (motor drive fn) ***')"

# --- return trap: restore hijacked-task context, force a context switch, disarm the hot hook ---
sysbus.cpu AddHook 0x30000100 "from Antmicro.Renode.Peripherals.CPU import RegisterValue as R; b=self.Bus; self.ErrorLog('9B: TRAP injected publish returned r0=0x{0:X}'.format(self.GetRegister(0).RawValue)); [self.SetRegister(i,R.Create(b.ReadDoubleWord(0x30000020+4*i),32)) for i in range(16)]; b.WriteDoubleWord(0xe000ed04,0x10000000); self.RemoveHooksAt(0x80e2d98)"

# --- injection: at the console busy-spin, ONLY in thread mode, publish door_unlock once ---
# saves r0..r15 to scratch, writes 8-byte payload {speed=0xC8, wait=0}, sets up
# sub_80c8f68("pid_motor"=0x0814F76C, "door_unlock"=0x0814F9C8, &payload=0x30000010, 8), LR=trap.
sysbus.cpu AddHook 0x80e2d98 "from Antmicro.Renode.Peripherals.CPU import RegisterValue as R; b=self.Bus; f=b.ReadDoubleWord(0x30000000); thr=((b.ReadDoubleWord(0xe000ed04)&0x1ff)==0); (None if (f!=0 or not thr) else [b.WriteDoubleWord(0x30000000,1)]+[b.WriteDoubleWord(0x30000020+4*i,self.GetRegister(i).RawValue) for i in range(16)]+[b.WriteDoubleWord(0x30000010,0xC8), b.WriteDoubleWord(0x30000014,0), self.SetRegister(0,R.Create(0x0814F76C,32)), self.SetRegister(1,R.Create(0x0814F9C8,32)), self.SetRegister(2,R.Create(0x30000010,32)), self.SetRegister(3,R.Create(8,32)), self.SetRegister(14,R.Create(0x30000101,32)), self.SetRegister(15,R.Create(0x080c8f68,32))])"

echo ">>> Booting U400 to running RTOS ..."
emulation RunFor "4.0"
echo ">>> Injecting door_unlock mbus publish; observing autonomous consumer wake -> actuator -> drive:"
emulation RunFor "1.5"
echo ">>> Done (see 9B: log lines above for the autonomous chain)."
quit
